From: Ruohang Feng <rh@vonng.com>
Subject: Allow bounded scheduling margins in asynchronous tests

Origin: vendor
Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-10-22

The PAUSE test's default one-second polling budget races the one-second
BLPOP timeout itself. Keep the command timeout and blocked-client assertion,
but allow one more second for the server cron and test client to observe it.

The diskless replication test sends SIGTERM and immediately checks for the
TLS disconnection log with a one-millisecond budget. Wait up to one second
for that same log; retain the replica count and data integrity assertions.

The timeout subcase can finish full sync before the test observes the load
log and sends SIGSTOP. Apply the existing bounded key-load delay there too,
so the test actually exercises a full-sync timeout and retains its original
log, surviving replica, and data integrity assertions.

Only tests change; server code and installed payload remain unchanged.

--- a/tests/unit/type/list.tcl
+++ b/tests/unit/type/list.tcl
@@ -2449,8 +2449,8 @@
         # now unpause the writes
         r client unpause
 
-        # client should time-out
-        wait_for_blocked_clients_count 0
+        # Allow scheduling margin beyond the BLPOP one-second timeout.
+        wait_for_blocked_clients_count 0 200 10
         
         $rd close
     }

--- a/tests/integration/replication.tcl
+++ b/tests/integration/replication.tcl
@@ -914,13 +914,14 @@
